---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy: SecureProspective"
  description="What SecureProspective collects, why, how long it is kept, and how to have it deleted."
>
  <Nav />

  <main id="main" class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-shell">
      <header class="legal-head">
        <p class="legal-kicker">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
        <p class="legal-lede">
          This policy covers secureprospective.com and the services we run for the advisors
          who work with us, including the social publishing tool at
          social.secureprospective.com. It says what we collect, why we collect it, who
          else sees it, and how to have it removed.
        </p>
      </header>

      <nav class="legal-index" aria-label="On this page">
        <a href="#who-we-are">Who we are</a>
        <a href="#what-we-collect">What we collect</a>
        <a href="#social-accounts">Connected social accounts</a>
        <a href="#platform-terms">Platform-specific terms</a>
        <a href="#how-we-use-it">How we use it</a>
        <a href="#sharing">Who else sees it</a>
        <a href="#retention">How long we keep it</a>
        <a href="#data-deletion">Deleting your data</a>
        <a href="#security">Security</a>
        <a href="#your-rights">Your rights</a>
        <a href="#children">Children</a>
        <a href="#changes">Changes</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>

      <section id="who-we-are" aria-labelledby="who-we-are-title">
        <h2 id="who-we-are-title">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          SecureProspective is an insurance marketing organization serving independent
          insurance and annuity producers. In this policy, "we" and "us" mean
          SecureProspective. "You" means anyone who visits our website, contacts us, or
          uses a service we operate for advisors.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are the controller of the personal information described here. Our contact
          details are in the <a href="#contact">Contact</a> section.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-we-collect" aria-labelledby="what-we-collect-title">
        <h2 id="what-we-collect-title">What we collect</h2>

        <h3>When you visit the website</h3>
        <p>
          Our hosting and network provider records standard request information, including
          IP address, browser and device type, the pages requested, and the time of the
          request. This is used to serve the site, keep it available, and defend it against
          abuse. We do not run advertising trackers or sell this information.
        </p>

        <h3>When you contact us</h3>
        <p>
          If you fill in a form or email us, we receive what you send: typically your name,
          email address, phone number if you give one, and the content of your message.
        </p>
        <p>
          The contact form also records which of the three lines you chose, the page you
          sent it from, and the IP address, browser string and country the request arrived
          with. Those last three are kept so we can tell a real enquiry from an automated
          one. The form is protected by Cloudflare Turnstile, a spam check that looks at
          how the request behaves rather than asking you to solve a puzzle, and that check
          runs before anything is stored.
        </p>

        <h3>When you have an advisor account</h3>
        <p>
          For advisors using services we host, we hold the account details needed to run
          them: name, email address, the organization you belong to, and the content you
          create in the service, such as drafted and scheduled posts and any media you
          upload.
        </p>

        <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
        <p>
          We do not collect client information on behalf of advisors through these tools,
          and we do not ask for Social Security numbers, account numbers, or health
          information anywhere on this website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="social-accounts" aria-labelledby="social-accounts-title">
        <h2 id="social-accounts-title">Connected social accounts</h2>
        <p>
          Our social publishing service lets an advisor connect their own social media
          accounts so they can schedule and publish their own posts. Connecting an account
          is always initiated by the advisor, and it is always their account, not ours.
        </p>
        <p>When you connect an account, we receive and store:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            an access token issued by that platform, which lets the service act on the
            account you authorized, and only in the ways you authorized;
          </li>
          <li>
            basic profile information used to identify the connection in the interface,
            such as the account or page name, its identifier on that platform, and its
            profile picture;
          </li>
          <li>
            the posts you publish through the service, and the engagement and reach
            statistics that platform reports back for them.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Access tokens are stored so the service can publish on your schedule without
          asking you to sign in again. They are held against your own organization in our
          database and are not shared with, or usable by, any other advisor.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use this access to publish the content you create, to read back the
          performance of those posts, and to show you which accounts and pages are
          connected. We do not read your private messages, we do not post anything you have
          not scheduled or approved, and we do not use your social data to build advertising
          profiles or to train machine learning models.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can disconnect an account at any time from within the service, and you can
          revoke our access from the platform's own settings. Disconnecting stops all future
          access immediately.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="platform-terms" aria-labelledby="platform-terms-title">
        <h2 id="platform-terms-title">Platform-specific terms</h2>

        <h3>Google and YouTube</h3>
        <p>
          Our use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
          >, including its Limited Use requirements. Where the service connects a YouTube
          account, it uses the YouTube API Services, and your use of it is also subject to
          the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">YouTube Terms of Service</a>
          and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
          You can revoke our access to your Google account at
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>Meta (Facebook and Instagram)</h3>
        <p>
          Where the service connects a Facebook Page, we access only the pages you select
          during authorization, and only for the permissions you grant. You can review and
          remove our access under Settings, then Business Integrations, in your Facebook
          account.
        </p>

        <h3>LinkedIn</h3>
        <p>
          Where the service connects a LinkedIn profile or company page, we access it only
          for the permissions you grant during authorization. You can remove our access
          under Settings, then Data Privacy, then Permitted Services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="how-we-use-it" aria-labelledby="how-we-use-it-title">
        <h2 id="how-we-use-it-title">How we use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To provide the services you asked for, including publishing what you schedule.</li>
          <li>To answer your questions and stay in contact with you about your work with us.</li>
          <li>To keep our systems available, secure, and free of abuse.</li>
          <li>To meet our legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it with advertisers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing" aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
        <h2 id="sharing-title">Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep the number of parties involved deliberately small. Information is shared
          only with:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            the social media platforms you choose to connect, when we act on your behalf at
            your instruction;
          </li>
          <li>
            infrastructure providers that host, deliver, or protect our services, acting on
            our instructions and not for their own purposes;
          </li>
          <li>
            professional advisors, or a regulator or law enforcement body, where we are
            legally required to do so.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Our hosted services run on infrastructure we operate and administer ourselves,
          rather than on a third-party software vendor's platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          Named plainly, the providers behind this website are Cloudflare, which hosts the
          site, stores what you send through the contact form, and runs the spam check on
          it, and Brevo, which delivers the notification email telling us your message
          arrived. Neither uses your information for its own purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-title">
        <h2 id="retention-title">How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Access tokens</strong> are kept while an account is connected, and
            deleted when you disconnect it or close your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Posts and scheduled content</strong> are kept while your account is
            open, so you have your own history.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Enquiries and correspondence</strong> are kept for as long as we are in
            contact with you and for a reasonable period afterwards.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Server and security logs</strong> are kept for a short operational
            period and then discarded.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="data-deletion" aria-labelledby="data-deletion-title">
        <h2 id="data-deletion-title">Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>You can have your information removed in either of these ways.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Disconnect an account yourself.</strong> In the social publishing
            service, open the channel and remove it. Its stored access token and profile
            details are deleted with it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Ask us.</strong> Email
            <a href="mailto:info@secureprospective.com">info@secureprospective.com</a> with
            the subject line <strong>Data deletion request</strong>, from the email address
            associated with your account, and tell us what you want removed: a single
            connected account, or your account and all of its content.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          We will confirm receipt and complete the deletion within 30 days, and we will tell
          you when it is done. If we are required by law to retain something, we will say so
          and tell you what and why.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security" aria-labelledby="security-title">
        <h2 id="security-title">Security</h2>
        <p>
          Traffic to our services is encrypted in transit. Access tokens and account
          credentials are held on systems we administer, with access limited to the people
          who need it to operate the service. No system is perfect, and we do not claim
          otherwise; if a breach affects your information, we will tell you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="your-rights" aria-labelledby="your-rights-title">
        <h2 id="your-rights-title">Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us for a copy of the information we hold about you, ask us to correct
          it, ask us to delete it, or object to a particular use of it. Write to
          <a href="mailto:info@secureprospective.com">info@secureprospective.com</a> and we
          will respond within 30 days. We will not treat you differently for exercising any
          of these rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children" aria-labelledby="children-title">
        <h2 id="children-title">Children</h2>
        <p>
          Our services are for insurance professionals and are not directed to children. We
          do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18. If you believe we have,
          contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
        <h2 id="changes-title">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of the page. Where a
          change materially affects how we handle your information, we will tell account
          holders directly rather than relying on you to notice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy, or about anything we hold, go to
          <a href="mailto:info@secureprospective.com">info@secureprospective.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem) 1.25rem clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
  }

  .legal-shell {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-head {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .legal-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .legal-head h1 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    opacity: 0.65;
  }

  .legal-lede {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-index {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  /* These sat 21px tall on a phone. The type stays as it is; the hit area is
     padded out around it so a thumb has something to land on. */
  .legal-index a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    opacity: 0.75;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .legal-index a:hover,
  .legal-index a:focus-visible {
    opacity: 1;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal-shell section + section {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .legal-shell h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .legal-shell h3 {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .legal-shell p,
  .legal-shell li {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-shell p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .legal-shell ul,
  .legal-shell ol {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-shell li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-shell a {
    color: inherit;
  }
</style>
